                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "About 100 minutes of cardiovascular work per week is good. This can be as simple as fast walking, or choose activities that are fun for you. 30 minutes of getting your heart rate to 60-80% of your maximum (220 minus your age), six out of seven days per week, can be an effective treatment for depression, as good as an antidepressant."
